;;; `(not ?s)` concluded of a stored `(eq k k)` stores `(not (eq k k))` and no `(false)` —
;;; M1f **W82**, register row `W82/eq-value-negation-concluded`, filed by S1f.7.10 (T1f.7.10.2,
;;; 2026-11-11).
;;;
;;; ── What this program is ──────────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; The probe that settled the value rule: two supposed equalities, `(h (eq k j))` and
;;; `(h (eq k k))`, and a rule that concludes the negation of each, `(not ?s)`. No
;;; candidate.
;;;
;;; ── The answer, by hand ───────────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; S1f.5.7 has a concluded `(not (eq …))` checked: `(not (eq k k))` is false, so were
;;; `(eq …)` a value root would be dead. It is no value: refused at the parse, on every
;;; command.
;;;
;;; ── What the engine answered ──────────────────────────────────────────────
;;;
;;; At `52e05fc1`, release: the program loads, and the rule stores `(not (eq k j))` and `(not
;;; (eq k k))`; no `(false)` is derived, root is alive and R is {∅}, exit 0 on every
;;; command.
;;; Refused at load since S1f.7.10 (T1f.7.10.3).

(relation h Claim :why "{?1} is supposed")
(h (eq k j)) (h (eq k k))
(rule r () :match (h ?s) :assert (not ?s) :why "not {?s}: it was only supposed")
(solve :hypothesis-relations ())
(query :goal (h ?s))
